        "original_id": "c663c4e8-a1db-5e29-87c7-78fc28dbde6a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Sikoryak, Samuel Beckett\n- Works: Masterpiece Comics, Crime and Punishment, Dostoyevsky Comics, Waiting for Godot, Waiting to Go, Carousel, White\n- Topics: comic adaptations, multimedia comics slide shows, literary parody\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Sikoryak was born in 1964 and is an American artist who usually signs his work as R. Sikoryak.\n- Robert Sikoryak specializes in making comic adaptations of literary classics.\n- Under the series title \"Masterpiece Comics,\" Robert Sikoryak created \"Crime and Punishment\" in the style of Bob Kane-era Batman as \"Dostoyevsky Comics,\" starring Raskol.\n- Under \"Masterpiece Comics,\" Robert Sikoryak also mixed \"Waiting for Godot\" with \"Beavis and Butt-Head\" to create \"Waiting to Go.\"\n- Since 1997, Robert Sikoryak has hosted \"Carousel,\" a long-running multimedia comics slide show presented at venues in the United States and Canada.\n- \"Waiting for Godot\" is a play by Samuel Beckett in which Vladimir and Estragon wait for someone named Godot, who never arrives, while talking and encountering three other characters.\n- The play \"White\" has been compared to \"Waiting for Godot\" and received critical acclaim.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4d4fbef9-7686-5837-bfc4-4d39296e5166",
        "text": "Page: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Robert Sikoryak (born 1964) is an American artist whose work is usually signed R. Sikoryak.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: He specializes in making comic adaptations of literature classics.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Under the series title \"Masterpiece Comics\", these include \"Crime and Punishment\" rendered in Bob Kane–era Batman style, becoming \"Dostoyevsky Comics\", starring Raskol; and \"Waiting for Godot\" mixed with \"Beavis and Butt-Head\", becoming \"Waiting to Go\".\nPage: Waiting for Godot. Sentence: Waiting for Godot ( ) is a play by Samuel Beckett, in which two characters, Vladimir and Estragon, wait for the arrival of someone named Godot who never arrives, and while waiting they engage in a variety of discussions and encounter three other characters.\nPage: Carousel (comics). Sentence: Carousel is a long-running multimedia comics slide show hosted by cartoonist Robert Sikoryak (\"Masterpiece Comics\") that has been presented in various venues in the United States and Canada since 1997.\nPage: White (play). Sentence: The play has been compared to \"Waiting for Godot\" and received critical acclaim.",
